    "faq": {
      "kicker": "FAQ",
      "title": "Frequently asked questions",
      "q1": "What is Rakhal?",
      "a1": "Rakhal is a smart dairy farm management platform — it brings cattle, milk, health, reproduction, expenses, and reports into one dashboard.",
      "q2": "Who can use Rakhal?",
      "a2": "Farm owners, managers, and workers — from small family farms to large commercial dairies.",
      "q3": "Can I track individual cattle?",
      "a3": "Yes. Every animal gets its own profile with breed, weight, status, photos, and full history.",
      "q4": "Can I track milk production?",
      "a4": "Yes. Log milk by session for every cow and see daily, weekly, and monthly production trends.",
      "q5": "Can I manage health and vaccination records?",
      "a5": "Yes. Report sickness, manage treatment plans, and get vaccine schedules with reminders.",
      "q6": "Does Rakhal support reproduction tracking?",
      "a6": "Yes. Track heat, insemination, pregnancy checks, and calving on a full reproduction timeline.",
      "q7": "Can I see profit and expense reports?",
      "a7": "Yes. Record income and expenses, and download profit/loss and other reports anytime.",
      "q8": "Is Rakhal suitable for small farms?",
      "a8": "Absolutely. Rakhal works for farms starting from around 20 animals — with a free way to begin.",
      "q9": "Can my staff use it?",
      "a9": "Yes. Invite team members with roles and permissions, so workers only see what they need.",
      "q10": "Do I need technical knowledge to use Rakhal?",
      "a10": "No. If you can use a smartphone, you can use Rakhal — it's Bangla-first and built for farmers."
    },
